{
  "info": {
    "name": "FaceAttend AI Server",
    "description": "ArcFace attendance system backed by MySQL — v6.0.0\n\n## Setup\n1. Set the `base_url` variable to your server address (e.g. `http://localhost:8000`).\n2. Set `admin_key` to your `ADMIN_API_KEY` environment variable value.\n3. Admin-protected endpoints (`POST /train-now`, `DELETE /register/student/:id`) require the `X-Admin-Key` header — it is pre-filled from the `admin_key` variable.\n\n## Flow\n1. Health check → confirm server is up\n2. Register → upload face image for a student\n3. Check Status → poll until completed\n4. Train Now → force-process pending queue (admin only)\n5. Verify → send a live face image to check attendance\n6. Logs → retrieve recent check-in logs\n7. Delete Student → remove student data (admin only)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "description": "Base URL of the AI server. Change to your deployed URL for production.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "admin_key",
      "value": "your-admin-api-key-here",
      "description": "Value of the ADMIN_API_KEY environment variable set on the server.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "student_id",
      "value": "S001",
      "description": "Student ID used across register / status / delete requests.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "device_id",
      "value": "ESP32-S3-01",
      "description": "Device ID of the ESP32-CAM module or client sending verification requests.",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Returns server status and database mode.\n\nExample response:\n```json\n{ \"status\": \"ok\", \"mode\": \"mysql\" }\n```"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/" }
              },
              "body": "{\"status\": \"ok\", \"mode\": \"mysql\"}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Registration",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Student",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "student_id",
                  "value": "{{student_id}}",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Alphanumeric, dashes and underscores only"
                },
                {
                  "key": "name",
                  "value": "John Doe",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Student display name (optional)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "files",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Face image file(s). Upload 1 photo."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["register"]
            },
            "description": "Upload one or more face images for a student. Non-blocking — images are queued for async processing.\n\n**student_id rules:** Only letters, numbers, `-` and `_` allowed.\n\nExample response:\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"Images queued for processing successfully\",\n  \"student_id\": \"S001\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"validation_checklist\": {\n    \"face_detected\": true,\n    \"single_face\": true,\n    \"database_match\": null\n  }\n}\n```"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Queued",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register" }
              },
              "body": "{\"message\": \"Images queued for processing successfully\", \"student_id\": \"S001\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"validation_checklist\": {\"face_detected\": true, \"single_face\": true, \"database_match\": null}}"
            },
            {
              "name": "400 Bad Request — Invalid student_id",
              "status": "Bad Request",
              "code": 400,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register" }
              },
              "body": "{\"detail\": \"Invalid student_id format. Only alphanumeric characters, dashes, and underscores are allowed.\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Check Registration Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/status/{{student_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["register", "status", "{{student_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Poll after registering to check processing status.\n\nPossible status values:\n- `pending` — still in queue\n- `processing` — being processed now  \n- `completed` — embeddings saved, student can be verified\n- `failed` — validation failed (see message)\n- `not_found` — no record for this student"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Completed",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/status/S001" }
              },
              "body": "{\"student_id\": \"S001\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"message\": \"Face extracted and saved successfully\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Pending",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/status/S001" }
              },
              "body": "{\"student_id\": \"S001\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"message\": \"Waiting for AI processing. Scheduled updates run daily at 19:00.\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Failed (no face detected)",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/status/S001" }
              },
              "body": "{\"student_id\": \"S001\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"message\": \"Please look at the camera\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Student  [Admin]",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Key",
                "value": "{{admin_key}}",
                "description": "Required — must match ADMIN_API_KEY on the server"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/student/{{student_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["register", "student", "{{student_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Permanently deletes a student's users record, registration queue records, and face embedding file.\n\nCheck-in log history is PRESERVED for auditing.\n\nRequires X-Admin-Key header."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Deleted",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "DELETE",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/student/S001" }
              },
              "body": "{\"message\": \"Student registration data deleted successfully\", \"student_id\": \"S001\"}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized",
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "DELETE",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/register/student/S001" }
              },
              "body": "{\"detail\": \"Unauthorized\"}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Training",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Force Train Now  [Admin]",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Key",
                "value": "{{admin_key}}",
                "description": "Required — must match ADMIN_API_KEY on the server"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/train-now?limit=50",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["train-now"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50",
                  "description": "Max pending queue items to process (default: 50)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Immediately processes pending registration queue items up to `limit`. Triggers face embedding extraction and saves the model.\n\nNormally runs on a schedule; use this to force it manually.\n\nRequires X-Admin-Key header."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Trained",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/train-now" }
              },
              "body": "{\"message\": \"Training completed for batch\", \"processed_students\": [\"S001\", \"S002\"], \"total_pending\": 0}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Nothing pending",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/train-now" }
              },
              "body": "{\"message\": \"No pending items to train.\", \"processed_students\": [], \"total_pending\": 0}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized",
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/train-now" }
              },
              "body": "{\"detail\": \"Unauthorized\"}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verification",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Verify Face (file upload)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Live face image (jpg/png)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/verify/face_recognition/{{device_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["verify", "face_recognition", "{{device_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Matches a live face photo against all registered embeddings. Logs a check-in entry on every call regardless of match result.\n\nUse `file` for binary upload (Postman/HTTP clients) or `image_base64` for base64 string (ESP32/Flutter)."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK — Match",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/verify/face_recognition/{{device_id}}" }
              },
              "body": "{\"match\": true, \"student_id\": \"S001\", \"similarity_score\": 0.92, \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-06T10:00:00\", \"message\": \"Welcome, S001!\", \"validation_checklist\": {\"face_detected\": true, \"single_face\": true, \"database_match\": true}}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — No match",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/verify/face_recognition/{{device_id}}" }
              },
              "body": "{\"match\": false, \"student_id\": null, \"similarity_score\": 0.21, \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-06T10:00:01\", \"message\": \"Employee data not found\", \"validation_checklist\": {\"face_detected\": true, \"single_face\": true, \"database_match\": false}}"
            },
            {
              "name": "200 OK — No face detected",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/verify/face_recognition/{{device_id}}" }
              },
              "body": "{\"match\": false, \"student_id\": null, \"similarity_score\": 0.0, \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-06T10:00:02\", \"message\": \"Please look at the camera\", \"validation_checklist\": {\"face_detected\": false, \"single_face\": false, \"database_match\": false}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Face (base64)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "image_base64",
                  "value": "<paste raw base64 JPEG string here>",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Raw base64 image string — no data: prefix. Used by ESP32 and Flutter."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/verify/face_recognition/{{device_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["verify", "face_recognition", "{{device_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Same as file upload but image is passed as a raw base64 string. This is the format used by ESP32 cameras and the Flutter mobile app. No data:image/jpeg;base64, prefix required."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Logs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Check-in Logs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/logs?limit=50",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["logs"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50",
                  "description": "Number of most-recent logs to return (default: 50)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the most recent check-in log entries, ordered newest-first.\n\nEach entry includes student_id, similarity_score, device_id, timestamp, and error_message."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/logs?limit=5" }
              },
              "body": "[{\"id\": 42, \"student_id\": \"S001\", \"similarity_score\": 0.91, \"device_id\": \"ESP32-S3-01\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-06T10:00:00\", \"error_message\": null}, {\"id\": 41, \"student_id\": null, \"similarity_score\": 0.18, \"device_id\": \"ESP32-S3-01\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-06T09:58:12\", \"error_message\": \"Employee data not found\"}]"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
